cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite a Nine Buckets issue, please cite the series as below."
title: "Nine Buckets — dispatches from a nine-account LLM fan-out"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/nine-buckets"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/nine-buckets"
date-released: "2026-09-15"
keywords:
  - llm-evaluation
  - model-disagreement
  - multi-model
  - reasoning
abstract: >-
  One question put to nine independent paid LLM accounts, each in its strongest
  reasoning mode, with the disagreement published rather than averaged away. A
  rail is vendor#account, not vendor, so separate subscriptions to the same
  vendor count as separate legs. Every issue reports which legs answered, where
  three or more legs agreed independently, where they split, the lonely
  position, and what came back as garbage. Failure rows are mandatory.
